## Epistemic discipline and fabrication spot-checks

- Every substantive paragraph, table row, and benchmark carries an epistemic tag; `uncertain` markers are used where the file admits absent evidence (extension transport/packaging, capability inventory, legacy deployment certification, operating counts). No bare concrete detail found without a tag.
- Claimed extractions verified against cited sources:
  - Nine connector verbs (`Describe` … `Contain`) match the `Operation` enum in `contracts/02-external-connector.yaml`.
  - `CF-ROUTE`, `CF-SYNC`, `CF-PROFILE`, `CF-STATE`, `CF-STRUCTURE`, `CF-INPUT`, `CF-IMAGE`, `CF-TIME`, `CF-EVIDENCE`, `CF-CAPS` all exist in `contracts/03-internal-browser-binding.yaml`; `LIFE-AXES`, `LIFE-DISPATCH`, `LIFE-SOURCE-CHECKS`, `LIFE-LATE-EVIDENCE`, `LIFE-MANUAL` and `EXT-DECLARE-NOT-ASSESS`, `EXT-PREPARATION-PIN`, `EXT-IDEMPOTENCY`, `EXT-RESUME`, `EXT-STATE-POLICY` all exist in their cited contracts.
