  - Resource baselines (12 tabs/shard, 3 tasks/account, back-pressure above 1,000, recycle at 500 pages) and all eight §8 benchmark targets (fingerprint stability, 500×150KB p95<200ms/RSS<2GB, 20% mutation >85% heal, 100×20 fairness, 500-page recycle, 20-session MFA, 2×-cap back-pressure, zero-match secret scan) match `4-circus-tent-arch.md` §§2/4/8–9. The file correctly frames these as fixture targets to be re-pinned, not measured results.
  - Provider handling (§3.4) names Crawl4AI/LiteLLM and refers to "named heal/vision providers" without freezing DeepSeek/model versions into portfolio constants — consistent with the arch blueprint and appropriately cautious.
- No fabricated citations, invented enumerations, or collapsed distinctions found. The "older blueprint's 'no Juggler layer' description does not govern" sentence follows the developer prompt's higher-authority Products statement; it is not a silent re-litigation. The "no further handoff amendment" declaration holds: no contract shape is changed through this PRD.

